class.description:
[INI] converts INI text to a [Dictionary] and back, and offers the [ConfigFile] API ([method set_value], [method get_value], [method get_sections], ...) on the same data. Parsing, errors, [method TextDataFormat.load] and [method TextDataFormat.save] come from [TextDataFormat]; [method parse_string] and [method stringify] work on data without an instance, [method serialize] and [method deserialize] on resources.
The data is a [Dictionary] of sections: each section name maps to a [Dictionary] of keys and values. Keys before the first [code][section][/code] header belong to the section [code]""[/code] and are written first, without a header. Lines starting with [code];[/code] or [code]#[/code] are comments. A section that appears twice is merged.
Values are written in Godot's [Variant] syntax, like [ConfigFile]: strings are quoted, numbers, [code]true[/code]/[code]false[/code] and [code]null[/code] are plain, other types use their constructor ([code]Vector2(1, 2)[/code]). With [member SerializerOptions.ini_value_style], values are plain text that other tools can read. Reading understands both forms; text that is neither a number, a boolean, [code]null[/code] nor Godot syntax is a [String].
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var ini = INI.new()
if ini.parse("version=2\n[video]\nsize=Vector2i(1280, 720)\nvsync=true\n") == OK:
	var data = ini.get_data()
	print(data[""]["version"]) # Prints 2
	print(data["video"]["size"]) # Prints (1280, 720)
else:
	print(ini.get_error_message()) # For example "Line 2: ..."; the line alone is ini.get_error_line().

print(INI.stringify({ "audio": { "volume": 0.5, "device": "Speakers" } }))
# [audio]
# volume=0.5
# device="Speakers"
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var ini = new Ini();
if (ini.Parse("version=2\n[video]\nsize=Vector2i(1280, 720)\nvsync=true\n") == Error.Ok)
{
	var data = ini.GetData();
	GD.Print(data[""].AsGodotDictionary()["version"]); // Prints 2
	GD.Print(data["video"].AsGodotDictionary()["size"]); // Prints (1280, 720)
}
else
{
	GD.Print(ini.GetErrorMessage()); // For example "Line 2: ..."; the line alone is ini.GetErrorLine().
}

var audio = new Godot.Collections.Dictionary { { "volume", 0.5 }, { "device", "Speakers" } };
GD.Print(Ini.Stringify(new Godot.Collections.Dictionary { { "audio", audio } }));
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Resource and files:[/b] [INI] is a [Resource] (see [TextDataFormat]). [code]load("res://x.ini")[/code] of a plain file returns an instance, while files with a [code]$type[/code] marker load as the serialized resource. Plain files load with the project default options. The instance methods [method TextDataFormat.load] and [method TextDataFormat.save] work like [method ConfigFile.load] and [method ConfigFile.save]: they do not use the resource cache and do not set [member Resource.resource_path]. In exported games [code]res://[/code] is read-only, so save to [code]user://[/code].
[b]Changes:[/b] changing the data ([member TextDataFormat.data] in the inspector, [member TextDataFormat.data], [method set_value], [method erase_section] ...) drops the kept parsed text, so comments and formatting of the file are lost on the next save. [member TextDataFormat.options] set to [code]null[/code] uses the project settings.
[b]ConfigFile and INI:[/b] the file extension [code].cfg[/code] is not claimed by [INI]; it stays with [ConfigFile]. [method set_value] with a [code]null[/code] value erases the key, and an emptied section is erased with it, like [ConfigFile]. Use [method to_config_file] and [method from_config_file] to convert between the two classes.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var ini = INI.new()
ini.set_value("video", "vsync", true)
ini.set_value("video", "size", Vector2i(1280, 720))
ini.save("user://settings.ini")

var loaded = INI.new()
if loaded.load("user://settings.ini") == OK:
	print(loaded.get_value("video", "vsync", false)) # Prints true
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var ini = new Ini();
ini.SetValue("video", "vsync", true);
ini.SetValue("video", "size", new Vector2I(1280, 720));
ini.Save("user://settings.ini");

var loaded = new Ini();
if (loaded.Load("user://settings.ini") == Error.Ok)
{
	GD.Print(loaded.GetValue("video", "vsync", false)); // Prints true
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] The static methods can be called from any thread. An [INI] instance should be used by one thread at a time.
